Local patch, not yet upstreamed: gates wry's WebViewBuilderExtDarwin import
behind target_os = "macos". The trait is only used inside an already-gated
block, but the import itself was unconditional, so stimpak-auth-window
fails to compile on non-macOS targets. Applies cleanly against
ncarrillo/superiority @ d34e9e1f43f6bca4f55937cfe76507fb56492c46.

diff --git a/stimpak/auth-window/src/main.rs b/stimpak/auth-window/src/main.rs
index 1f48c4c..d2fc8c7 100644
--- a/stimpak/auth-window/src/main.rs
+++ b/stimpak/auth-window/src/main.rs
@@ -19,7 +19,9 @@ use tao::{
     window::WindowBuilder,
 };
 use url::Url;
-use wry::{WebViewBuilder, WebViewBuilderExtDarwin as _};
+use wry::WebViewBuilder;
+#[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
+use wry::WebViewBuilderExtDarwin as _;

 /// its own cookie jar, distinct from the app's and from every other webview on
 /// the machine. a supporting crate must not sign someone in off a session it
